course: dictionary
lesson: 14050
title: A name, a people and a city
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words start with a capital letter and name a special thing, such as a person, a place or a people. Mari is one of these. Look at the clues in the sentence to find out which Mari it is.
explain: «The Mari live near the Volga river in Russia.» Here Mari names a people, because people live somewhere and are called by a name.
explain: «Mari is related to Finnish and Hungarian.» Here Mari names a language, because languages can be related to each other.
explain: «I met a girl called Mari at the park.» Here Mari is a girl's name. Do not mix it up with «Mary», which is a different name, or «marry», which is a verb meaning to wed.
fact: Mari is a proper noun, so it starts with a capital letter.
fact: «Mari» is the name of a people who live mainly in the Mari El Republic in Russia, by the Volga river.
fact: «Mari» is also the name of their language, which is related to Finnish and Hungarian.
fact: «Mari» was an ancient city in what is now Syria, famous for clay tablets with old writing.
fact: «Mari» is a girl's name in several countries, such as Estonia, Finland and Japan.
exercise: «The Mari live by the Volga river in Russia.» What are the Mari? | A river | *A people | A mountain | A type of food
exercise: «Mari is related to Finnish and Hungarian.» What does Mari mean here? | *A language | A month of the year | A girl's name | A city in Syria
exercise: «Thousands of clay tablets were found at the ancient city of Mari.» In which country was the ancient city of Mari? | Estonia | *Syria | Russia | Japan
test: «Mari is a kind and clever girl in my class.» In this sentence, what is Mari? | A people | *A girl's name | A language | An ancient city
test: Where do most of the Mari people live? | *Russia | Hungary | Syria | Japan
exam: Which sentence uses Mari as a language? | «Mari was an ancient city in Syria.» | «I met a girl called Mari.» | *«Mari is related to Finnish and Hungarian.» | «The Mari live by the Volga river.»
